# The same steps as scripts/init-and-deposit.sh (.bat), which runs them through the CLI.
# A family member is born first; its id is the ownerId of the piggybank.
# Deposits and withdrawals address the ownerId, as in the commands.
# Select the dev environment and log in first; keycloak_setup.md explains http-client.private.env.json.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@ownerId = 89a7e903-4c29-4fba-ac52-253292126794

### Log in as a parent: the access token goes into access_token for the requests below
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{client-id}}&client_secret={{client-secret}}&username={{parent}}&password={{password}}&scope=openid

> {%
    client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### A family member is born (201): the grandparents project it as a grandchild
POST {{baseUrl}}/family-members
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "familyMemberId": "{{ownerId}}",
  "firstName": "Emma",
  "lastName": "Peeters"
}

### Create a piggybank (201): the grandparents make a savings promise
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerId": "{{ownerId}}"
}

### Deposit money (200 with the updated balance)
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks/{{ownerId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 20
}

### Deposit money again
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks/{{ownerId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 20
}

### Withdraw money (200 with the updated balance; refused when the balance is too low)
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks/{{ownerId}}/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 10
}

### Deposit money a third time: the savings promise of 50 is reached
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks/{{ownerId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 20
}

### List all piggybanks with their owner and balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Without a token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks
Accept: application/json

### Log in as a grandparent
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{client-id}}&client_secret={{client-secret}}&username={{grandparent}}&password={{password}}&scope=openid

> {%
    client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### List the grandchildren the grandparents projected from the born events
GET {{baseUrl}}/grandchildren
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### A grandparent deposits money too
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks/{{ownerId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 5
}

### A grandparent may not withdraw (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/piggybanks/{{ownerId}}/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 5
}
